       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Peter Matthew Eichman",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Ab97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" data-account-id=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" accountid=\"557058:b97337af-3737-473c-9779-44d498499536\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Harshakumar Ummerpillai</a>, it depends on how you have deployed fcrepo. The fcrepo-audit module is compiled into the fcrepo-webapp-plus WAR file by default. However, you can disable it by making sure this line is not present (or commented out) in your spring configuration:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-xml\">\r\n<span class=\"code-tag\">&lt;bean class=<span class=\"code-quote\">\"org.fcrepo.audit.InternalAuditor\"</span>/&gt;</span></pre>\n</div></div>",
     "created": "10/Nov/17 12:16 PM",
